From f82cf3f85c473efec5604b21d76f57a7f513e3ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: farrizdesignpro1339 <garenafreefiremax1339@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:34:02 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: sc27xx_fgu: also accept sgm41513-charger

The Unisoc SC2730 PMIC fuel gauge looks for a charger power supply
by name (sc27xx_charger_supply_name[]) to report the battery status.
On the Redmi A5 / POCO C71 (serenity) the charger is an external
SGM41513 (power supply "sgm41513-charger", patch 0045), so no supply
was found and the driver logged "get charger status error.".

Add "sgm41513-charger" to the list.

Beleg 14.11. (Redmi A5): /sys/class/power_supply/sc27xx-fgu/status
zeigt am PC-Kabel "Charging", ohne Kabel "Discharging" (vorher kannte
die Akkuanzeige den Ladezustand nicht). "get charger status error"
nur noch 2x ganz frueh beim Start (FGU startet vor dem Ladetreiber),
danach keine mehr.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W8YQkFAqgbw689knydrHtG
---
 drivers/power/supply/sc27xx_fuel_gauge.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/sc27xx_fuel_gauge.c b/drivers/power/supply/sc27xx_fuel_gauge.c
index 125b6e2ef..068bcd7da 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/sc27xx_fuel_gauge.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/sc27xx_fuel_gauge.c
@@ -144,6 +144,7 @@ static const char * const sc27xx_charger_supply_name[] = {
 	"sc2720_charger",
 	"sc2721_charger",
 	"sc2723_charger",
+	"sgm41513-charger",
 };
 
 static int sc27xx_fgu_adc_to_current(struct sc27xx_fgu_data *data, s64 adc)
-- 
